	After Nethack's main program is compiled, the levels are built
from data files using special level-building tools.  It's great:  you
can design new levels without knowing how to program.  The new levels
don't break save-file compatibility:  you can still use Hearse, or
add levels while a game is in progress.  It's easy to distribute pre-
built levels to anyone using the same version of Nethack as you.  And
you don't have to compile Nethack's main program.  

	So, here, we're thinking in terms of what can be done with
the existing level-building tools.  You're thinking of actual code
changes, which would allow a lot more, yes, but has a sharply higher
pain-in-the-butt value.  


